  "findings": [
    {
      "status": "measured: all23 existing audit metadata",
      "finding": "No full seven-stage success under any of the four frozen protocols. No second required cup is lifted >25mm in any group. Counts are metadata observations, not new scoring."
    },
    {
      "status": "measured: four selected default/overlap first-case streams",
      "finding": "Required first cup has zero Robot-contact ticks and max positive z displacement about 1.5um. No object lifts >1.22mm. Three of these cases touch B without bilateral contact or lift; the remaining default reverse has no object Robot contact. These sampled failures occur before successful grasp; no-contact is not a hand-distance measurement."
    },
    {
      "status": "measured: seven cases with attachment activation files",
      "finding": "Earliest measured attachment acquisition is always D: five overlap and two warm. All seven have actual thumb+opposing contact and measured lift>=15mm at activation. Four are forward/A-first cases, three are reverse/D-first cases. Event logs alone cannot exclude an earlier unassisted grasp; warm forward full raw confirms A is never contacted."
    },
    {
      "status": "measured: warm24 raw two cases",
      "finding": "Both have actual D bilateral contact + >25mm lift before manager attachment (ticks1617 vs attach1633; tick1720 vs attach1735). Forward should first manipulate A but never contacts A; D is correctly released onto the pan and remains there, so ordered phase stays0 while unordered auxiliary phase reaches1."
    },
    {
      "status": "measured: warm24 reverse raw and original scores",
      "finding": "D is released on pan and completes phase1. It later reaches pad_D physically, but the r1 pad completion event still has Robot contact; neither released protocol nor v1.1 completes pad return. The policy regrabs D and sends it to the pan again; at480s D is upright, released and on pan, while C has zero Robot contact throughout. This is not a dropped-cup failure and not a pan XY tolerance failure."
    },
    {
      "status": "measured: existing overlap reverse r005/r006 metadata only",
      "finding": "Both complete D pan and ownpad under v1.1 (2 phases), but C has zero Robot contact over the complete trace and after D return. r005 later has D displaced from ownpad at end; r006 ends on original topple rule. Neither advances to the second distinct cup."
    }
  ],
